## Solana Security Checklist

### Account Validation
- [ ] All accounts verify signer when required
- [ ] Account owners are validated
- [ ] Account data matches expected relationships (has_one/constraint)
- [ ] Initialization can only happen once
- [ ] Duplicate mutable accounts are prevented
- [ ] Account types have unique discriminators

### PDA Security
- [ ] Canonical bump seeds used (find_program_address)
- [ ] PDAs include unique identifiers (no sharing)
- [ ] Bump stored and verified on subsequent calls

### CPI Security
- [ ] Target programs validated before CPI
- [ ] Signer seeds properly scoped
- [ ] Return values checked

### Account Lifecycle
- [ ] Accounts properly closed (data zeroed)
- [ ] Rent exemption maintained
- [ ] Rebirth attacks prevented

### Math & Logic
- [ ] Checked arithmetic used
- [ ] No integer overflow/underflow
- [ ] Division by zero prevented
